msgid ""
"title: Quickstart\n"
"description: A quickstart guide for the Shaded lightcones Qiskit addon (qiskit-addon-slc)\n"
msgstr ""
"title: Permulaan pantas\n"
"description: Panduan permulaan pantas untuk addon Qiskit Shaded lightcones (qiskit-addon-slc)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide demonstrates a minimal working example of the `qiskit-addon-slc` package. It calculates a shaded lightcone to reduce the sampling cost of probabilistic error cancellation (PEC).\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menunjukkan contoh minimum yang berfungsi bagi pakej `qiskit-addon-slc`. Ia mengira shaded lightcone untuk mengurangkan kos pensampelan pembatalan ralat probabilistik (PEC).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC mitigates gate noise by sampling from a quasiprobability decomposition of the inverse noise channel. Its sampling cost grows with every error term it must mitigate; however, not every error affects the observable equally. An error outside the observable's causal lightcone cannot influence the measured expectation value, and even within the lightcone, some errors are more detrimental than others. A shaded lightcone quantifies this by bounding the effect each Pauli error term has on the observable. Truncating the error terms with the smallest effect shrinks the noise model that PEC has to mitigate, reducing sampling cost in exchange for a small, bounded bias.\n"
msgstr "PEC memitigasi hingar gate dengan mensampel daripada penguraian kuasi-kebarangkalian bagi saluran hingar songsang. Kos pensampelannya meningkat dengan setiap terma ralat yang perlu dimitigasi; namun, tidak semua ralat memberi kesan yang sama kepada observable. Ralat di luar lightcone kausal observable tidak dapat mempengaruhi nilai jangkaan yang diukur, dan walaupun di dalam lightcone, sesetengah ralat lebih memudaratkan daripada yang lain. Shaded lightcone mengkuantifikasikan ini dengan menyempadankan kesan setiap terma ralat Pauli terhadap observable. Memangkas terma ralat yang kesannya paling kecil akan mengecilkan model hingar yang perlu dimitigasi oleh PEC, mengurangkan kos pensampelan sebagai pertukaran kepada bias kecil yang bersempadan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see how to build a realistic workflow and run on quantum hardware, check out the [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](/tutorials/pec-with-shaded-lightcones) tutorial on IBM Quantum Platform.\n"
msgstr "Untuk melihat cara membina aliran kerja yang realistik dan menjalankannya pada perkakasan kuantum, lihat tutorial [Pembatalan ralat probabilistik dengan shaded lightcones](/tutorials/pec-with-shaded-lightcones) di IBM Quantum Platform.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Prepare the inputs for SLC {#1-prepare-the-inputs-for-slc}"
msgstr "1. Sediakan input untuk SLC {#1-prepare-the-inputs-for-slc}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, build a 10-qubit Trotterized transverse-field Ising circuit and choose a single-qubit $Z$ observable on the middle qubit.\n"
msgstr "Mula-mula, bina litar model Ising medan melintang 10-qubit yang di-Trotter dan pilih observable $Z$ qubit tunggal pada qubit tengah.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart/extracted-outputs/0fff4e37-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart/extracted-outputs/0fff4e37-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SLC operates on the noisy two-qubit-gate layers of the circuit. Here we use ``samplomatic`` to group the gates into annotated boxes and attach a noise-injection annotation to each two-qubit layer. SLC requires every noisy box to have a unique `modifier_ref`, which `inject_noise_strategy=\"individual_modification\"` provides; with samplomatic's default strategy, the bounds come out wrong or their computation never finishes. `generate_noise_model_paulis` then enumerates the Pauli error terms of every unique noisy layer.\n"
msgstr "SLC beroperasi pada lapisan gate dua-qubit yang berhingar bagi litar. Di sini kita menggunakan ``samplomatic`` untuk mengumpulkan gate ke dalam kotak beranotasi dan melampirkan anotasi suntikan hingar pada setiap lapisan dua-qubit. SLC memerlukan setiap kotak berhingar mempunyai `modifier_ref` yang unik, yang disediakan oleh `inject_noise_strategy=\"individual_modification\"`; dengan strategi lalai samplomatic, sempadan yang diperoleh salah atau pengiraannya tidak pernah selesai. `generate_noise_model_paulis` kemudian menyenaraikan terma ralat Pauli bagi setiap lapisan berhingar yang unik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Compute the shaded lightcone {#2-compute-the-shaded-lightcone}"
msgstr "2. Kira shaded lightcone {#2-compute-the-shaded-lightcone}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The shaded lightcone is assembled by assigning a scale to each Pauli error term in the noise model based on how much effect it has on the observable expectation value. These scales are derived from each error term's forward and backward error bounds (described below), as well as its error rate:\n"
msgstr "Shaded lightcone dibina dengan menetapkan skala kepada setiap terma ralat Pauli dalam model hingar berdasarkan sejauh mana kesannya terhadap nilai jangkaan observable. Skala ini diperoleh daripada sempadan ralat hadapan dan belakang bagi setiap terma ralat (diterangkan di bawah), serta kadar ralatnya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`compute_forward_bounds` evolves each error term *forward* to the end of the circuit to bound its effect on the observable measured there.\n"
msgstr "`compute_forward_bounds` mengembangkan setiap terma ralat *ke hadapan* hingga akhir litar untuk menyempadankan kesannya terhadap observable yang diukur di situ.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`compute_backward_bounds` evolves each error term *backward* to the start of the circuit to bound its effect on the initial state.\n"
msgstr "`compute_backward_bounds` mengembangkan setiap terma ralat *ke belakang* hingga permulaan litar untuk menyempadankan kesannya terhadap keadaan awal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge_bounds` combines the two into a single bound per error term. Each bound is scaled by the term's error rate. These rates typically come from a noise learning experiment (such as `NoiseLearnerV3`); this guide uses random rates for simplicity.\n"
msgstr "`merge_bounds` menggabungkan kedua-duanya menjadi satu sempadan bagi setiap terma ralat. Setiap sempadan diskalakan mengikut kadar ralat terma tersebut. Kadar ini lazimnya datang daripada eksperimen pembelajaran hingar (seperti `NoiseLearnerV3`); panduan ini menggunakan kadar rawak untuk kemudahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the shaded lightcone visualization below, each box is shaded by how strongly the errors at that site can affect the observable.  Bright boxes carry the largest bounds, while boxes that fade to the background contain error terms that have little effect on the calculation -- these errors are natural candidates to drop from the noise model. The values in the visualization below represent sums of the error bounds of all Pauli errors at that site, which is why some of the values grow larger than ``2.0``, the bound for any single Pauli error.\n"
msgstr "Dalam visualisasi shaded lightcone di bawah, setiap kotak dilorekkan mengikut sejauh mana ralat pada tapak itu boleh menjejaskan observable.  Kotak terang membawa sempadan terbesar, manakala kotak yang pudar ke latar belakang mengandungi terma ralat yang kesannya kecil terhadap pengiraan -- ralat ini calon semula jadi untuk digugurkan daripada model hingar. Nilai dalam visualisasi di bawah mewakili jumlah sempadan ralat bagi semua ralat Pauli pada tapak itu, sebab itulah sesetengah nilai menjadi lebih besar daripada ``2.0``, sempadan bagi sebarang ralat Pauli tunggal.\n"

